 "engineNeeds": [
  {
   "need": "decode font chosen by a register field",
   "keys": "display.decode as an object: {\"field\": \"CTRL.HEXA\", \"values\": {\"1\": \"hex\", \"0\": \"codeB\"}} (a field value not listed uses the first entry), alongside the string form",
   "why": "ICM7218A/B: ID6 of the control word picks hexadecimal (1) or Code B (0) for the whole display; ICM7218C/D: pin 9 picks them (below). Today the A/B and C/D devices decode hex only (CTRL.HEXA is stored but unused), so Code B codes 10-15 (- E H L P blank) show as hex A-F."
  },
  {
   "need": "three-level input pin",
   "keys": "pins.levels entry with \"tri\": true, e.g. {\"pin\": \"HEXA/CODEB/SHUTDOWN\", \"field\": \"MODE9.LVL\", \"tri\": true}: the field gets 0 for a driven low, 1 for Z (floating), 2 for a driven high (field 2 bits wide); copied whenever the pin changes and at power-on",
   "why": "ICM7218C/D pin 9: high = hexadecimal, floating = Code B, low = shutdown (Renesas p.4-5). `levels` reads Z as 0, so a floating pin cannot be told from a low one. With both needs: decode {\"field\": \"MODE9.LVL\", \"values\": {\"2\": \"hex\", \"1\": \"codeB\"}}, shutdown \"MODE9.LVL=0\" (the C/D then need a 2-bit register MODE9 with field LVL, reset 1)"
  },
  {
   "need": "(optional) shutdown to Z",
   "keys": "display.shutdownZ: true on digits",
   "why": "the real outputs are high impedance in shutdown (leakage specs, Renesas p.5); today shutdown drives the inactive level, which lights nothing but is not Z"
  },
  {
   "need": "(finding, not a new feature) [NAME] in an input pattern is never applied",
   "keys": "docs/parts-format.md \u00a7 Patterns says `[NAME]` in `in` puts the bits into the register or field; backend/src/models/converter.c captures() only reads CVT_CAP tokens and nothing writes CVT_REF tokens of `in`",
   "why": "A write command `\"in\": \"0 [DIG1.V]\"` loads the loader but stores nothing (found by bench). The ICM7218 devices use capture letters and `set` instead (`in` \"vvvv\", `set` {\"DIG1.V\": \"v\"}). The other devices that use `[REG]` in `in` (converter.json CONFIG, DEVICE_CFG, CMR3...) are probably affected."
  }
 ],
 "notes": "Four devices ICM7218A (common anode) / B (common cathode) / C / D, 25 parts. The A/B are NOT serial: ID0-ID7 bytes with MODE (control word) and WRITE, written one after another (the brief's 'serial' is the Maxim cover wording). Modeled: control word (shutdown ID4, decode ID5, data coming ID7), 8 sequential data bytes with blanking while loading and ignored extra writes, hex decode and No Decode (ID6 a, ID5 b, ID4 c, ID3 e, ID2 g, ID1 f, ID0 d), decimal point lit by ID7 low (stored inverted in DIGn.DP), C/D random access DA0-DA2 with ID3-0 and ID7, digit order D1 D7 D8 D6 D4 D3 D2 D5 at 500 us. Not modeled: Code B (engineNeeds), the C/D three-level pin 9 incl. shutdown (engineNeeds), Maxim-only bank select and single digit update of A/B (spec), interdigit blanking, Z outputs in shutdown. Power-up state is not in the sheets (A/B: shutdown, C/D: zeros). Datasheets: icm7218-renesas (verified: the Renesas URL answers a PDF of 759428 bytes = the local file). icm7218-icm7228-maxim has NO entry: analog.com timed out for every request from this machine, including a known-good Analog Devices sheet, so the Maxim parts (ICM7218xIPI, xIQI and their + forms, manufacturer Analog Devices) carry no datasheet key; please check from Safari (Analog Devices' ICM7218 page) and, if hosted, add the id icm7218-icm7228-maxim and the key to those 17 parts, or add the parts to the 'maker no longer hosts' table in docs/parts-format.md. Footprints reused: CDIP-28-600 (CERDIP), PDIP-28-600 (body in the Maxim drawing 13.72 x 37.34 mm vs 13.21 x 36.32 mm in the footprint; leads identical), PLCC-28 (the Maxim sheet has no PLCC drawing; the pin numbers equal the DIP ones). Parts: the Renesas CERDIP names AIJI/BIJI/CIJI/DIJI + R5254 forms (DIJIR5254 flagged obsolete), the Maxim PI/QI names and their + forms (AIQI+T too); main thread prunes by stock. Tests: bench icm7218_test.c (53 checks; needs logic_test(icm7218_test) in CMake); library_check passes; listing_check and trace_check fail only with 'extra part (not in the golden)' for the 25 new parts."
